We have I, III and IV currently, so the issue is II, your Usage Decides 
cmavo. I don't think this will fly either, but whatever, this can be 
discussed.

> #Function words are a closed set, but 'closed' never
> #means 'hermetic'. And this is revising the lexer, not necessarily the
> #grammar itself.
> One might go further and say "this is revising the lexer, and 
> necessarily
> not revising the grammar itself". The Lojban design as it stands allows
> for new cmavo, but not for new selmaho.

I'm OK with that. Of course, we both understand by that what linguists 
understand by grammar, which is that the lexer (lexicon) and the parser 
(grammar) are distinct entities, and changes to one are separate from 
changes to the other.

